WEBVTT

00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:06.465
Ah!

00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:09.593
[electricity crackles]

00:00:10.261 --> 00:00:11.637
[dramatic music plays]

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.473
[grunts, shouts]

00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:19.603
[pants] Honestly, Wolf,
what made you think this would work?

00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:22.398
Who says it didn't?

00:00:23.107 --> 00:00:25.985
Like you said, it's not about the action,

00:00:26.068 --> 00:00:27.569
it's about the distraction.

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:30.239
[chuckles]

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:33.492
Hey, genius,
the watch controls the shuttle,

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:34.994
not the magnet.

00:00:35.828 --> 00:00:37.329
You get it. [clicks tongue]

00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:38.414
She gets it.

00:00:38.998 --> 00:00:40.207
[beeps, chimes]

00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:42.918
[controls beeping]

00:00:43.002 --> 00:00:44.128
[shuttle rumbles]

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.342
[Piranha grunts] Got it!

00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:52.177
[strained] You sure about this?

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:53.429
Trust me, chico.

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:56.098
Tuna power!

00:00:58.142 --> 00:01:01.395
-[air hisses]
-[shouting]

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:06.984
I got it!

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:08.861
[shuttle rumbles]

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:13.073
Well done, boys.
Webs, tell me you're ready.

00:01:13.157 --> 00:01:14.616
Lining it up, Wolfie.

00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:19.913
[Wolf] Nice work, kid.

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:20.998
No.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.083
You wanna see a power move, Kitty?

00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:26.378
-This is a power move.
-[watch beeps]

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:34.303
[grandiose music plays]

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:42.269
[gold clinking]

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:52.988
[people cheering]

00:01:57.284 --> 00:02:00.371
[chuckles] It's fine. [chuckles]

00:02:01.497 --> 00:02:04.083
-[gasps]
-Hello! Need a hand?

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:06.001
I got you, Snakey Cakes!

00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:08.879
[Snake] Aw, Sugar Beak.

00:02:09.505 --> 00:02:12.383
And you said you weren't into me.

00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:15.886
Why would you believe anything I say?

00:02:17.763 --> 00:02:18.764
No!

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:24.436
How do you expect to get back
to Earth without a shuttle?

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.063
At least there's an Earth to go back--

00:02:26.647 --> 00:02:29.108
You destroyed my beautiful plan.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.694
[growls, grunts]

00:02:33.445 --> 00:02:34.655
[coughing]

00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:37.658
-[shouts]
-[gasps]

00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:47.626
-[screams]
-[grunts]

00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:53.882
What did I tell you
about messing with my friends?

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:55.676
-What-- How did you--
-Wolf, we got--

00:02:55.759 --> 00:02:57.845
[romantic music plays]

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.896
We tried to stop her from posting--

00:03:16.113 --> 00:03:18.240
Wow. What happened to
medium friendly?

00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:21.243
[giggles] Well, good thing
I'm not the governor anymore, huh?

00:03:21.785 --> 00:03:23.120
[chuckles]

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.496
Ugh.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.622
Gross.

00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:27.124
About time!

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.042
-[both] Guys!
-Whoa! Diane?

00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:30.544
What are you doing here?

00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:32.504
[chuckles] Just happened to be
orbiting the Earth.

00:03:32.588 --> 00:03:33.589
Thought I'd drop by.

00:03:33.672 --> 00:03:35.215
-[Piranha] Yeah!
-[all cheer]

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:36.341
We did it, baby!

00:03:37.301 --> 00:03:38.635
I feel the love. Like, I feel it.

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:42.014
I hear about the famous
Bad Guys all my life.

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:44.057
But now, I get it.

00:03:45.142 --> 00:03:46.602
-[shuttle rattles]
-[alarm blares]

00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:47.811
[electronic voice] Alert.

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:53.484
Alert.

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:56.820
Alert.

00:03:57.571 --> 00:03:59.573
It Is a massive system failure!

00:03:59.656 --> 00:04:01.575
-[electronic voice] Alert.
-We're falling out of orbit!

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:03.327
[dramatic music plays]

00:04:07.372 --> 00:04:08.415
[all groan]

00:04:08.499 --> 00:04:10.501
-[grunts]
-[grunting]

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.838
- I think this is it, Wolfie.
-We're doomed!

00:04:14.922 --> 00:04:16.131
One last hug, everybody?

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:19.927
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hang on. Don't talk like that.

00:04:20.552 --> 00:04:23.680
Sure, it's-- it looks...
[voice cracks] Yeah, it's bad.

00:04:23.764 --> 00:04:25.432
Yeah, okay. It's bad.

00:04:25.516 --> 00:04:27.559
Sure, we're hurtling
towards Earth in a tin can

00:04:27.643 --> 00:04:28.936
staring squarely into the face of death.

00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:31.688
Sure, our blood may boil,
our bones may liquefy

00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:34.775
but if there's one thing
that I know about this crew,

00:04:34.858 --> 00:04:37.861
it's that we never ever give up.

00:04:37.945 --> 00:04:41.823
Because we have something
that's stronger than fear,

00:04:41.907 --> 00:04:44.284
-stronger than even gravity!
-[inspirational music plays]

00:04:44.368 --> 00:04:45.577
And that's hope.

00:04:45.661 --> 00:04:47.454
Yeah. Hope.

00:04:47.538 --> 00:04:48.789
[Wolf] That's hope.

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:52.668
We're gonna land this thing,

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:55.420
or we're gonna die try--

00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:56.838
[bell tolling]

00:04:56.922 --> 00:04:58.549
[mourners sniffling]

00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:02.261
[mournful music playing]

00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:05.472
[Luggins] What those guys,

00:05:05.556 --> 00:05:08.600
those brave, beautiful guys did up there

00:05:08.684 --> 00:05:13.230
saving the world
from a 24-carat catastrophe...

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.817
And despite all the rejection
and suspicion,

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.986
all the tiny humiliations,

00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:21.029
they did it for us!

00:05:21.697 --> 00:05:24.449
They didn't do it for the fame
or for the glory.

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.577
They did it for us.

00:05:27.286 --> 00:05:29.079
They weren't just good guys,

00:05:30.497 --> 00:05:32.082
they were my best friends.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:38.171
And I would give anything
to arrest them just one more time.

00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:40.257
[all sobbing]

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:46.555
This one's for you, Wolfie.

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.349
[sighs]

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:53.937
/, for one, am outraged that
it took an evil space magnet

00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:59.526
for people to realize that the Bad Guys
were worthy of our love all along.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.321
But it's foo late,
because now they're dead.

00:06:04.573 --> 00:06:07.993
Ironically, the only survivors
were the perpetrators of the heist,

00:06:08.076 --> 00:06:11.622
including the super criminal
known as the Phantom Bandit,

00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:15.167
while a second escape pod
was, tragically, empty.

00:06:16.793 --> 00:06:18.170
[sighs]

